{"title":"Previously Funded Projects","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Previously Funded Projects","page-layout":"full","toc":false},"headingText":"Previously funded projects","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n::: hero-slideshow\n<img src=\"images/humans nature/01 MBC team shows BSF larvae to farmers (Nov 2024).jpg\" class=\"hero-slide active\"/> <img src=\"images/humans nature/08 Working frass into the soil, Tahiana farm (Dec 2025).jpg\" class=\"hero-slide\"/> <img src=\"images/humans nature/10 BSF fly cage over pond (Apr 2025).jpg\" class=\"hero-slide\"/> <img src=\"images/humans nature/11 Farmers with BSF products (Nov 2024).jpg\" class=\"hero-slide\"/> <img src=\"images/humans nature/DSCN3267.jpg\" class=\"hero-slide\"/> <img src=\"images/humans nature/Credit Ranjana Bhatta.jpg\" class=\"hero-slide\"/> <img src=\"images/humans nature/Phoebe and Basanta credit Prakash Basnet.png\" class=\"hero-slide\"/>\n:::\n\n```{=html}\n<script>\n  let slideIndex = 0;\n  const slides = document.querySelectorAll(\".hero-slide\");\n\n  setInterval(() => {\n    slides[slideIndex].classList.remove(\"active\");\n    slideIndex = (slideIndex + 1) % slides.length;\n    slides[slideIndex].classList.add(\"active\");\n  }, 5000);\n</script>\n```\n\n\nWe are so proud to have sponsored two projects so far:\n\n::::: image-grid\n::: image-card\n<img src=\"images/Madagascar farms/03 Dried BSF larvae at a small farm (Nov 2024).jpg\"/>\n\n<h2>Black Soldier Fly microfarms in Madagascar</h2>\n\n<p>This project developed research, guides and training for local farmers to use soldier fly farming (BSF) as a simple and low-cost way to turn waste and invasive plants into valuable resources like animal feed, organic fertilizer and nutritious food.</p>\n\n<p>**Project leader:** Dr Brian Fisher</p>\n\n<p>**Project website:** [Madagascar Bio](https://www.madagascarbio.org/bsf-farms.html)</p>\n:::\n\n::: image-card\n<img src=\"images/croc/adult gharial holding.png\"/>\n\n<h2>Gharial conservation in Nepal</h2>\n\n<p>The Himalayan Gharial Project is a conservation and research initiative dedicated to understanding why the gharials remain Critically Endangered in Nepal, and how to support their long-term recovery.</p>\n\n<p>**Project leader:** Dr Phoebe Griffith</p>\n\n<p>**Project website:** [Himalayan Nature](https://www.himalayannature.org/works/projects/himalayan-gharial-project/)</p>\n:::\n:::::\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n::: hero-slideshow\n<img src=\"images/humans nature/01 MBC team shows BSF larvae to farmers (Nov 2024).jpg\" class=\"hero-slide active\"/> <img src=\"images/humans nature/08 Working frass into the soil, Tahiana farm (Dec 2025).jpg\" class=\"hero-slide\"/> <img src=\"images/humans nature/10 BSF fly cage over pond (Apr 2025).jpg\" class=\"hero-slide\"/> <img src=\"images/humans nature/11 Farmers with BSF products (Nov 2024).jpg\" class=\"hero-slide\"/> <img src=\"images/humans nature/DSCN3267.jpg\" class=\"hero-slide\"/> <img src=\"images/humans nature/Credit Ranjana Bhatta.jpg\" class=\"hero-slide\"/> <img src=\"images/humans nature/Phoebe and Basanta credit Prakash Basnet.png\" class=\"hero-slide\"/>\n:::\n\n```{=html}\n<script>\n  let slideIndex = 0;\n  const slides = document.querySelectorAll(\".hero-slide\");\n\n  setInterval(() => {\n    slides[slideIndex].classList.remove(\"active\");\n    slideIndex = (slideIndex + 1) % slides.length;\n    slides[slideIndex].classList.add(\"active\");\n  }, 5000);\n</script>\n```\n\n# Previously funded projects\n\nWe are so proud to have sponsored two projects so far:\n\n::::: image-grid\n::: image-card\n<img src=\"images/Madagascar farms/03 Dried BSF larvae at a small farm (Nov 2024).jpg\"/>\n\n<h2>Black Soldier Fly microfarms in Madagascar</h2>\n\n<p>This project developed research, guides and training for local farmers to use soldier fly farming (BSF) as a simple and low-cost way to turn waste and invasive plants into valuable resources like animal feed, organic fertilizer and nutritious food.</p>\n\n<p>**Project leader:** Dr Brian Fisher</p>\n\n<p>**Project website:** [Madagascar Bio](https://www.madagascarbio.org/bsf-farms.html)</p>\n:::\n\n::: image-card\n<img src=\"images/croc/adult gharial holding.png\"/>\n\n<h2>Gharial conservation in Nepal</h2>\n\n<p>The Himalayan Gharial Project is a conservation and research initiative dedicated to understanding why the gharials remain Critically Endangered in Nepal, and how to support their long-term recovery.</p>\n\n<p>**Project leader:** Dr Phoebe Griffith</p>\n\n<p>**Project website:** [Himalayan Nature](https://www.himalayannature.org/works/projects/himalayan-gharial-project/)</p>\n:::\n:::::\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"link-external-newwindow":false,"self-contained-math":false,"format-resources":[],"notebook-links":true},"pandoc":{"standalone":true,"wrap":"none","default-image-extension":"png","